        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Tillandsia tricholepis is a plant species of flowering plant in the family Bromeliaceae. It is native to Bolivia, Paraguay, Argentina, and Brazil. A curiosity of its morphology is that it is a land-dwelling plant which has no stomata, a characteristic it shares only with Stylites (or Isoetes) andicola."
